# Fiat Panda first generation three-door, 1980-2003 (UK 1981-1995).
#
# The original Giugiaro Panda: the boxy, flat-glazed city car with the
# corrugated lower door pressings, the simple upright cabin and the
# washable interior. UK imports ran from May 1981 to June 1995. The 4x4 is a
# taller, wider variant and is not separately represented.
# https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fiat_Panda
#
# Dimensions 3.380 x 1.460 x 1.445 m, wheelbase 2.160 m (launch figures).
#
# Shape reference: the flank is measured from a level side photograph
# of a Panda 34 scale model, not a full-size car. The measurements
# are calibrated to the published full-size dimensions above. Front
# and rear three-quarter photographs of a full-size 1984 Panda 45 S
# check the nose, hatch and lower panels. Two 1995 UK CLX photographs
# show the same shell with later trim.
#
# Colours: grade (d); no UK chart was found. White, red, blue and green are
# plain names. Weights 9, 8, 7, 6, total 30, provisional.
#
# Speed 130 km/h. Comfort 55/413, on the line 330 + 1.5 x 55: a simple,
# upright, noisy cabin. Classes 0,1.
# Dates are road presence: 1981 intro, retires staggered 2010-2013.
#
# Metres master: citycars/4.5/fiat-panda-1.blend. Interchange:
# citycars/4.5/fiat-panda-1.dae. References:
# citycars/references/fiat-panda-1/ (Wikimedia Commons full-size
# photographs and the supplied panda-mk1-side-model.jpg).
#
# Accepted deviations: the flank is measured from a level side view of a Panda 34
# scale model, not from a photograph of a full-size car; that is recorded as the
# side reference. The round lamp elements sit in simplified housings. At 128 px
# the boxy three-door body, flat glass and near-vertical tail read as a Panda 141.


obj=citycar
name=FiatPanda1(White)
copyright=JamesPetts

DistributionWeight=9
intro_year=1981
intro_month=5
retire_year=2013
retire_month=6
speed=130
class=0,1
maximum_comfortable_journey_minutes=55
maximum_tolerable_journey_minutes=413

